ightsizing actions, operating-model implementation and related advisory costs."]},{"type":"p","children":["Order intake \u0026 BACKLOG"]},{"type":"p","children":["Backlog totaled €3.9 billion, representing 7.9% organic growth year-on-year driven by Resilience and Places and providing continued support for future revenue growth. In Resilience, order intake was supported by Water in the US and Netherlands, Power in Germany and strong activity in Brazil, including Mining \u0026 Critical Minerals. In Places, major semiconductor awards drove strong order intake, while the Architecture business within Real Estate \u0026 Development in Canada remained challenging. In Mobility, order intake reflected the timing of awards. Our strong backlog continues to provide visibility for future growth."]},{"type":"p","children":["BALANCE SHEET \u0026 CASH FLOW"]},{"type":"p","children":["Free Cash Flow was €131 million in the third quarter, compared with €80 million in Q3’25, reflecting the seasonal pattern and continued discipline on billing and cash collection. Days Sales Outstanding was 65 days, compared with 73 days in Q3’25, while Net Working Capital was 12.4% of annualized gross revenues. Net debt decreased to €910 million at the end of the third quarter, from €1,042 million at the end of the second quarter of 2026."]},{"type":"p","children":["OPERATIONAL HIGHLIGHTS"]},{"type":"p","children":["RESILIENCE"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["(38% of net revenues)"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["in € millions "]},{"type":"table-data-cell","